{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The extra distance was the rider's own idea, not the driver's: MSG-00109-001, sent by RIDER at 18:22:06 — fifty-six seconds after the meter started at 18:21:10 and before the vehicle could have left the optimal corridor — reads 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min' and carries a platform-resolved waypoint_hint at Jurong Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT), with the driver replying 'ok can, i wait at the phv pickup point' at 18:22:31. That satisfies limbs (a), (b) and (c) of POL-RD-04: it is a rider instruction, it is timely, and it names an actionable place. The excess attributable to it is therefore excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "payload.messages[0].waypoint_hint",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04's corroboration test is met on the cleanest possible artifact: the gps_trace has 207 fixes at a 10-second interval with 100% coverage, no gaps and a max_gap_sec of 0.0, and it places the vehicle stationary 38 m from the Jurong Point PHV pickup point carried on MSG-00109-001's waypoint_hint for 366 seconds — comfortably inside the 200 m proximity test. The waypoint is taken from the resolved field, not geocoded from general knowledge, exactly as the clause demands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the rider-requested Jurong Point leg is excluded under POL-RD-04, no excess survives the POL-RD-01 gate. The corroborated waypoint was the driver's only stop, it is the sole non-optimal movement in the record, and the rider's own message shows it was planned before the trip began in earnest. No deviation is established against the driver on the adjusted route, so the rider's claim for the contested SGD 12.00 is not supported and the outcome on the fare is NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03: payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 stand as they are.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the road caused this detour. EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING — the identifier is retained with no payload and admissibility weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so no traffic_advisory names any segment the optimal route uses and no external event can be pointed to. The absence is itself citable, and it matters here: with no closure and no advisory, the only cause of the extra distance in the record is the rider's instruction, which is the POL-RD-04 case and not a POL-RD-03 exoneration. I disclose the artifact's MISSING status and its 0.0 weight rather than presenting it as evidence of a road condition.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00109-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The burden rule is discharged on the driver's side. The rider met her initial POL-RD-08 burden — EV-TRIP-00109, EV-GPS-00109 and EV-FARE-00109 all carry trip TRP-00109 and the same pickup window — so the burden shifted to the driver, and he answers it the way POL-RD-08 requires: a specific artifact, EV-CHAT-00109, and a specific clause, POL-RD-04, with GPS corroboration from EV-GPS-00109. That is not a general assertion that traffic was bad; it is a named instruction at a named place, verified on the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-FARE-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-04"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The percentage excess (over 115% of the 6.4 km optimal, on the trace distance that POL-RD-01 makes governing) would normally trigger the POL-RD-06 uplift. It does not here. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 511 — a ratio of 0.0, below the 0.05 test, and a count below the 3-flag test — so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) applies, and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows. I cite only the two fields POL-RD-06 names, as POL-GEN-01 requires; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the trailing-window figure the clause asks for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Separately from the refund question, and whether or not any deviation is found, the driver is owed money under the compensation limb of POL-RD-04. The fare_breakdown bills the rider for distance_charged_km of 9.60 while the gps_trace records trace_distance_km of 13.76 — a shortfall of 4.16 km, well past the 1.0 km gate. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is 3.12, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 as the policy requires, giving SGD 3.15, inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. I ask for a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling under POL-GEN-03 with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both carrying SGD 3.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
